Do not format nlohmann::json values with fmt 10

fmt 10.2.1, the version in scarthgap, cannot format a nlohmann::json value, or a fmt::join() over a
nlohmann::json array:

rosidlcpp_typesupport_fastrtps_c.cpp:152:76:   required from here
fmt/core.h:2593:45: error: 'fmt::v10::detail::type_is_unformattable_for<nlohmann::json_abi_v3_11_3::basic_json<>, char> _' has incomplete type
fmt/core.h:1604:7: error: static assertion failed: Cannot format an argument. To make type T formattable provide a formatter<T> specialization

Join the namespaces with a small helper and pass the type names as std::string.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Rob Woolley <rob.woolley@windriver.com>
---
--- a/src/rosidlcpp_typesupport_fastrtps_c/rosidlcpp_typesupport_fastrtps_c.cpp
+++ b/src/rosidlcpp_typesupport_fastrtps_c/rosidlcpp_typesupport_fastrtps_c.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,20 @@
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
 
+namespace {
+// fmt 10 cannot format a nlohmann::json array through fmt::join(), so join the strings by hand.
+auto join_namespaces(const nlohmann::json& namespaces, const std::string& separator) -> std::string {
+  std::string result;
+  for (const auto& ns : namespaces) {
+    if (!result.empty()) {
+      result += separator;
+    }
+    result += ns.get<std::string>();
+  }
+  return result;
+}
+}  // namespace
+
 auto get_includes(const nlohmann::json& message) -> nlohmann::json {
   nlohmann::json includes_json = nlohmann::json::array();
 
